We introduce a novel approach to evaluating grammatical errors in writing, focusing on both the frequency and significance of these mistakes. Our method utilizes a combination of a language model and a classifier to assess error severity, and we demonstrate its effectiveness by applying it to a large dataset of corrected sentences. Our results show that this approach can accurately identify grammatical errors and outperforms existing methods, and we also explore its potential applications in real-world contexts, such as evaluating student writing. Our code and data are available for public use. 

